@*
    Our Values (2026-08-03) — docs/03_PageBlueprints.md "Page — Our Values".
    Title/description/canonical/OG/AboutPage schema come from
    ViewData["Seo"] + ViewData["SeoPageType"], set in ValuesController.Index
    via ISeoService — see _Layout.cshtml's <head> and
    SeoStructuredDataViewComponent.

    Page flow (project owner's 2026-08-03 approval, narrower than
    03_PageBlueprints.md's fuller section list): Breadcrumb → Hero Banner
    (Standard) → Introduction → Core Values → Quality Commitment. Projects
    CTA / Partner Logos / Footer / Floating Contact Button are already
    global (_Layout.cshtml); Social Media is out of this milestone's scope
    per the project owner — same "global pieces need no section of their
    own" reasoning as About Us's Foundation phase.

    Hero Banner uses a dedicated placeholder banner image
    (wwwroot/images/hero/values-placeholder.svg), matching About Us/Project
    Detail's "always has its own banner" precedent rather than the neutral
    gradient HeroBannerStandard falls back to.

    Introduction / Core Values / Quality Commitment each reuse existing
    building blocks only (Section Header, Information Card's Grid layout)
    — no new Value Card/Introduction Card component, per project owner's
    explicit instruction — see ValuesIntroductionViewComponent /
    CoreValuesViewComponent / QualityCommitmentViewComponent.
*@

@{
    var breadcrumbTrail = new List<AncinInsaat.ViewComponents.BreadcrumbItem>
    {
        new() { Label = "Değerlerimiz" }
    };
}
@await Component.InvokeAsync("Breadcrumb", new { trail = breadcrumbTrail })

@await Component.InvokeAsync("HeroBannerStandard", new
{
    heading = "Değerlerimiz",
    subheading = "Yarım asra yaklaşan yolculuğumuzda bize yön veren ilkeler.",
    backgroundImageUrl = "/images/hero/values-placeholder.svg"
})

@await Component.InvokeAsync("ValuesIntroduction")

@await Component.InvokeAsync("CoreValues")

@await Component.InvokeAsync("QualityCommitment")
